+`pane.marks` returns up to `limit` (default 100, max 256) recent shell commands
+delimited by OSC 133 semantic prompt marks, oldest first. Each mark has
+`prompt_row` (133;A), `output_row` (133;C), `end_row` (133;D), `exit_code`,
+`started_at_ms` and `finished_at_ms` (when Herdr observed C and D), and
+`command` (the shell input cells between B and C). Rows are the cursor row when
+each mark was processed, counted from the oldest retained scrollback row; set
+`pane.scroll` `offset_from_bottom` to `total_rows - viewport_rows - row` to show
+a row at the top. Commands whose prompt row has left the scrollback are
+dropped. Shells report marks only with shell integration enabled.
+
 `layout.export` returns a portable tab layout tree. Omit `tab_id` and `pane_id`
 to export the active tab, pass `tab_id` to export that tab, or pass `pane_id` to
 export the tab containing that pane.
